# The pinned nidara-desktop release this repo packages.
#
# There used to be three more pins here — ASTAL_REF, AGS_REF and APPMENU_REF —
# kept in lockstep with nidara-desktop/install.sh, which carried its own copy of
# each. Nidara v0.8.0 removed the last of those upstreams (the application host,
# the bundler, every service and the PAM layer are native now), so install.sh has
# no `*_REF` at all and this file is the only place a pin lives.
#
# There used to be a second one too — NIDARA_ISO_REF — because `nidara-release`
# carried the PRODUCT's version and that number had to lock to a nidara-iso tag.
# The product no longer has a version and nidara-iso is no longer tagged, so the
# package moved into packages/ here and the pin went with it (2026-08-30).
#
# build-repo.sh builds `nidara-desktop` (and `nidara-installer`, its split twin)
# from this release TAG, with the PKGBUILD that ships INSIDE the tag
# (packaging/nidara/) — nothing about the desktop's layout is committed here.
#
# ⚠️ These pins (NIDARA_REF, and YAY_AUR_REF below) are the only things here that
# can be out of date without anything failing: the three packages in packages/
# are built from the working tree and are always current.
#
# Release runbook: tag nidara-desktop first, THEN point this at the new tag (one
# line) and push — CI fetches the tag's tarball, so a pin ahead of the tag fails.
# Empty = skip (releases predating the packaging switch).
NIDARA_REF=v0.12.1

# yay, which nidara-system depends on so the AUR is available on a Nidara machine
# (decided 2026-09-13). A COMMIT of https://aur.archlinux.org/yay.git, not a
# version: the AUR PKGBUILD at that commit is what gets built, checksums
# verified. To update yay, point this at a newer commit of that repository.
# YAY_REBUILD=N forces a rebuild of the same commit as pkgrel <rel>.N — for when
# pacman bumps libalpm's soname and the published yay stops starting. See the
# yay block in build-repo.sh for why it is otherwise never rebuilt.
YAY_AUR_REF=cb43f84828ab4f9700f7c6f9c6d7a923d4cfaff0
YAY_REBUILD=
